{
  "_comment": "Single source of truth for the power-effect display/resolution registry (PROD6B-2). The engine include_str!s this (crates/coh_math/src/effect_registry.rs) to resolve per-power granted buff/debuff magnitudes into three-tier values. The vendored beta keeps its own hand-authored EFFECT_REGISTRY (src/data/core/effect-registry) with NO sync gate against this file — the generated-copy gate this comment used to describe no longer exists, so a rule changed here must be carried there by hand if the beta ever ships again (WS14). App-glue describing how an exported effect key is interpreted for display, not binary-derived, so hand-authored here. Presentation-only fields (Tailwind colorClass, renderAs) stay beta-side and are deliberately absent. Field meanings: format = display unit; enhancementAspect = which per-power enhancement bonus scales it (absent = not enhanceable); strengthAspect = which build-wide global/+Strength key scales it, when that differs from enhancementAspect (the game reads Strength at the mod's OWN attrib offset, while a boost may enhance several attribs at once — absorb is enhanced by Healing IOs but takes Absorb Strength, never Heal Strength; absent = same as enhancementAspect); calculation = buff/debuff base-rate face used only on the table-less fallback path; baseMultiplier = percent multiplier (default 100); flatPercentPerScale = fixed percent per scale point, ignoring any AT-table reference the data carries; canBeByType = value may be a by-type object (collapse to first value); expandByType = a by-type value expands into one row per type; scalarFromTablePercent = a NON-by-type value resolves via the table-base resistance-percent path. typeLabels = per-type row-label vocabulary for an expanded by-type row (beta TYPE_LABELS_FULL); mezLabels = the same for an expanded protection row (beta MEZ_LABELS); byTypeKeys = the lowercased key set that identifies a value as a by-type object rather than a scaled effect (beta isByTypeObject). valueFromTable = a value-format effect resolves scale x AT-table at the BUILD level into an amount (heal/absorb HP); maxHpFractionPercentForm = an authored maxHPFraction, or a scale on a *_Ones table, means a fraction of Max HP and displays as percent.",
